count":1},{"category":"Wine & Spirits","historical_business_count":1},{"category":"Restaurants","historical_business_count":8},{"category":"Food Delivery Services","historical_business_count":0}],"history":[{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Beer, Food, Restaurants, Wine & Spirits","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"T3hRVrL3Yyy27iOvvKW8Ig","review_id":"6TXVGo0qVimTkPTO0T2qSg","date":"2013-01-07T20:17:47","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9616933465003967,"text_excerpt":"You need to check the website to see where they're at, but this is some darn good barbecue. I still love The Joint and Walker's Cochon de Lait Po-Boy but NOLA Smokehouse is doing just about everything right. Burnt Ends were fantastic on flavor - only issue is that they had way too much fat on the pieces I was served (about half overall), though I saw some other portions which appeared to be virtually all meat so I think it was just bad luck. Pulled pork was great - especially with the vinegar BBQ sauce - and brisket was tender and excellent. Even the sides of potato salad and cole slaw were really good. I hope this becomes a more regular thing at Killer Po-Boys, but regardless of where yo..."},{"business_id":"T3hRVrL3Yyy27iOvvKW8Ig","review_id":"RXxi5vd1jwyvwirtKXw52A","date":"2012-09-27T20:04:34","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9586260318756104,"text_excerpt":"Very good BBQ. We finally have a solid BBQ scene with the joint leading the pack but with saucy's, squeal, and Nola smokehouse all providing solid options after living in the BBQ barren lands of voodoo BBQ for too long. Nola smokehouse is probably my favorite after the joint. Just wish they were open longer and not just sundays and mondays and didn't run out of food so fast. Also well priced."},{"business_id":"T3hRVrL3Yyy27iOvvKW8Ig","review_id":"cQetEOZOuFBlbCoLKJP-Kg","date":"2012-10-04T21:08:24","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.947062611579895,"text_excerpt":"Really good BBQ. It is also served at the Avenue Pub on Sundays and Mondays. The hole hog smoked pork is to die for. The smoked sausage is awesome, as is the side of pasta salad. The different BBQ sauces they make are great. Everything reminds me of great North Carolina BBQ. I need to try this place a couple more time for a 5 star review, but damn, one of the best places in New Orleans for BBQ without a doubt."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
